---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import { packages, story, versionOf } from "../data/site";

const questions = [
  ["What is qyl?", "An analytical engine for agents. The Collector ingests OpenTelemetry traces, logs and metrics, stores them per project in DuckDB and computes the answers: triage, failure context, comparisons and fix verification. The MCP server hands those answers to the agent as structured results. qyl has no dashboard or other interface for people."],
  ["Who built qyl?", `${story} Alexander Nachtmann (ancplua) develops qyl and operates the hosted service.`],
  ["What does qyl store?", "The Collector retains OTLP traces, logs and metrics in DuckDB for 30 days by default (QYL_RETENTION_DAYS), plus the annotations, saved queries and failure status agents create through the write tools. Profiles are not supported."],
  ["How does an agent connect?", "Claude (claude.ai, Claude Desktop, Cowork and the mobile apps) and ChatGPT add https://mcp.qyl.at/mcp as a custom connector or MCP server. Claude Code and Codex install the qyl plugin from the ancplua-anthropic or ancplua-openai marketplace. The Claude and OpenAI APIs pass a qyl access token to their MCP tool. Locally, npx qyl-mcp-server --stdio connects an agent to a Collector started with qyl up."],
  ["Do I need the hosted endpoint?", "No. qyl up runs the Collector on your machine, and the stdio server reads it without an account. The hosted endpoint serves accounts the operator has mapped to a Collector project on api.qyl.at; support sets up access."],
  ["Which MCP revisions does the server answer?", "Protocol 2026-07-28, through the MCP TypeScript SDK v2. Clients on the 2025 revisions that open with initialize are still answered through the SDK's stateless fallback, with the same tools and checks."],
  ["Can a tool change my telemetry?", "No. The read tools are annotated read-only. The write tools change only annotations, saved queries and failure status: create_annotation and create_saved_query are marked as non-destructive writes, and update_annotation, update_saved_query, update_failure_status and delete_record as destructive, so a host can ask before each call. The hosted server also requires qyl:write or qyl:delete for them."],
  ["What happens when the Collector is unavailable?", "The call fails with a typed error that names a stable code and whether a retry can succeed. qyl never substitutes demonstration data for collector evidence."],
  ["How is the hosted endpoint authenticated?", "qyl is an OAuth 2.1 resource server backed by Auth0. The host performs Authorization Code with PKCE for https://mcp.qyl.at/mcp with the OAuth client registered for it in qyl's Auth0 tenant. qyl:read is required on every request; the write tools also need qyl:write (create, update) or qyl:delete (delete_record), and a call without it gets an insufficient_scope challenge to reconnect and allow that scope."],
  ["Can qyl notify an agent?", "Yes, through MCP Events on the hosted endpoint. A client that implements them, such as ChatGPT in Work chats, subscribes to trace.error, optionally for one service, and receives a signed webhook when a new trace with an error span reaches its project."],
  ["Which versions does this site describe?", `${packages.map((entry) => `${entry.name} ${entry.version}`).join(", ")}. The qyl tool, qyl-mcp-server, Qyl.Api.Sdk and Qyl.Orchestration are released together at one version from one revision of ANcpLua/qyl. The footer of every page states the versions, and the getting-started table links each one to the registry that serves it.`],
  ["Where do the telemetry attribute names come from?", "One Weaver registry holding the upstream OpenTelemetry conventions, the gen-ai conventions and qyl’s own attributes as YAML. The C# and TypeScript constants are generated from the same resolved registry, with generated outputs committed and checked for drift. qyl-owned instrumentation uses those constants; the Collector applies the rename table generated from the same registry plus four legacy aliases, and counts the attributes its capture policy denies on qyl.collector.attributes.dropped."],
  ["Does Qyl.Api.Sdk require Native AOT?", `It is built for it. Qyl.Api.Sdk ${versionOf("Qyl.Api.Sdk")} is an MSBuild SDK for a Native AOT ASP.NET Core API: it turns PublishAot on unless the project sets it, turns reflection-based JSON off, and generates XML output at compile time behind [GenerateXml] rather than reflecting at runtime. AddQylApi registers validation, problem details and the OpenAPI document in one call.`],
] as const;
---

<BaseLayout title="FAQ" description="Direct answers about what qyl is, who built it, how agents connect, what it stores, protocol support, safety, Events and hosted authentication.">
  <section class="page-hero">
    <div class="site-shell">
      <span class="eyebrow">FAQ</span>
      <h1 class="page-title">Questions worth answering precisely.</h1>
      <p class="lede">No roadmap theatre. These answers describe the software that exists now.</p>
    </div>
  </section>
  <section class="editorial-section">
    <div class="site-shell faq-layout">
      <div><span class="eyebrow">Current release</span><h2 class="section-title">The operating model, without the brochure.</h2></div>
      <div class="faq-list">
        {questions.map(([question, answer], index) => (
          <details open={index === 0}>
            <summary><span class="faq-number">Q{index + 1}</span><span>{question}</span><span class="faq-toggle" aria-hidden="true"></span></summary>
            <div class="faq-answer"><p>{answer}</p></div>
          </details>
        ))}
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
